From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 19:25:15 +0200
Subject: MIPS: intel-mips: allow selecting the FRITZ!Box 7590 built-in DTB

Add the 7590 as a third entry in the built-in-DTB choice, plus its dtb-y
rule. This is the whole of the kernel-side multi-board work: the choice
already delivers one built-in board DTB per kernel build, which is what
this platform needs and what the other MIPS platforms do -- lantiq, ralink
and bmips all have the same shape, the last with sixteen entries.

One build per board is not a cost the choice imposes, either. These two
boards differ in RAM size and flash geometry, so they need separate images
regardless of how the DTB is selected. Runtime selection would need
something the platform does not have: the dies are identical, so a chip ID
cannot tell a 7590 from the 7580 that shares its SoC, and EVA hands the
kernel no DTB to select from (fw_arg0 = 0) -- it is the built-in blob or
nothing. Should a reviewer ask for runtime selection anyway, the route is
UHI handoff via get_fdt(), which is code-read and untested.

CONFIG_CMDLINE stays shared. Both boards want the same arguments today, so
nothing forces the MIPS_CMDLINE choice off BUILTIN_EXTEND, under which the
DT bootargs are not read at all.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>

diff --git a/arch/mips/boot/dts/intel-mips/Makefile b/arch/mips/boot/dts/intel-mips/Makefile
index 3d2176ca6a28..f30e986f42b7 100644
--- a/arch/mips/boot/dts/intel-mips/Makefile
+++ b/arch/mips/boot/dts/intel-mips/Makefile
@@ -1,3 +1,4 @@
 # SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
 dtb-$(CONFIG_DTB_INTEL_MIPS_GRX500)	+= easy350_anywan.dtb
 dtb-$(CONFIG_DTB_INTEL_MIPS_FRITZ7560)	+= seale_avm_fritz7560.dtb
+dtb-$(CONFIG_DTB_INTEL_MIPS_FRITZ7590)	+= seale_avm_fritz7590.dtb
diff --git a/arch/mips/intel-mips/Kconfig b/arch/mips/intel-mips/Kconfig
index 70ddb9473870..f0891200a1fe 100644
--- a/arch/mips/intel-mips/Kconfig
+++ b/arch/mips/intel-mips/Kconfig
@@ -19,6 +19,10 @@ config DTB_INTEL_MIPS_FRITZ7560
 	bool "AVM FRITZ!Box 7560"
 	select BUILTIN_DTB
 
+config DTB_INTEL_MIPS_FRITZ7590
+	bool "AVM FRITZ!Box 7590"
+	select BUILTIN_DTB
+
 endchoice
 
 endif
